WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.940
Varys: Aegon the Unworthy legitimized all
of his bastards on his deathbed.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.220
Inevitably, the greatest of these, Daemon
Blackfyre, declared himself the rightful heir

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.230
and ignited yet another war for the crown.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:19.140
After much bloodshed, Daemon was killed by
an alliance of his half-brothers on the Redgrass

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.420
Field.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.119
All the same, his descendants continued to
threaten the Targaryens until half a century

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:31.029
later, when Barristan the Bold slew Maelys
the Monstrous on the Stepstones, extinguishing

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.360
Daemon's line.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:38.800
Aegon, the Fourth of His Name, is remembered
by history as "The Unworthy".

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.989
Quite a feat considering the other kings of
Westeros.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:49.290
But even in a family not known for equanimity,
Aegon stands out for spiteful incompetence.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:54.829
He tore apart the realm simply because he
couldn't rule himself, much less Westeros.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:01:00.520
As a young prince, Aegon's wit made him beloved
at court and won him forgiveness for youthful

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:06.039
indiscretions, but the cold steel of the Iron
Throne didn't temper his passions.

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:10.829
King Aegon proclaimed that if he had to spend
his days being pricked by a thousand swords,

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:14.909
he'd spend his nights pricking others with
his one.

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:19.561
Lords sent their daughters from court so they
would not catch the king's eye whilst other

00:01:19.561 --> 00:01:24.039
lords summoned their daughters to court so
they would.

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:29.840
The only woman in whom he took no pleasure
was his sister and wife Naerys, even after

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.159
she gave him a son and heir, Daeron.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:36.819
Perhaps Aegon was jealous of her supposed
love for his brother, the legendary hero Prince

00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:39.060
Aemon the Dragonknight.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.719
Aegon was most certainly jealous of him.

00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:47.529
Not of his bravery or honor, but how young
maidens swooned and cried at the songs about

00:01:47.529 --> 00:01:48.529
him.

00:01:48.529 --> 00:01:53.020
But most likely, Aegon disregarded his wife
and son because he chafed at restraints of

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.249
any kind.

00:01:54.249 --> 00:01:59.030
Be they the bonds of marriage or patrimony
or even reason.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:04.459
When Prince Daeron objected to his father's
foolish plan to invade Dorne, Aegon incited

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:10.780
a lickspittle lord to accuse the queen of
adultery with Aemon, making Daeron illegitimate.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.920
Prince Aemon defended the queen's honor in
trial by combat.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.480
But while the lord's claim publicly died with
him, no sword can kill a rumor.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:27.120
Out of spite and pique, Aegon had seeded doubt
into his own heir's claim to the throne, which

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:33.040
bore bitter fruit with the birth of another
son, the bastard Daemon Waters, by the king's

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.689
own cousin.

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:40.569
Raised in the Red Keep on account of his mother's
royal blood, Daemon grew tall and powerful

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:46.359
and excelled at all the marshal skills that
men wrongly value in leaders.

00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:51.709
Instead of protecting his own heir from a
rival, Aegon knighted Daemon at twelve and

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:57.280
shocked the realm by bestowing on him the
Conqueror's own Valyrian steel sword.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.230
He even let the boy renounce his common bastard's
name and take the Targaryen sword's name for

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.730
his own, becoming Daemon Blackfyre.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:10.650
Still, though a name can change, blood can't.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.599
And Daeron was Aegon's only trueborn son.

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:16.079
Until he wasn't.

00:03:16.079 --> 00:03:22.060
On his deathbed, Aegon forever earnt his epithet
by legitimizing all his bastards, from the

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.610
baseborn sons to the great bastards of noble
ladies, including Daemon.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:35.989
Fittingly, Aegon's last act was to thrust
himself into the realm and seed chaos.

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:40.870
A Targaryen without self-restraint may have
led Westeros to the brink of ruin, but the

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.690
highborn pushed it over.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:48.650
Though Daeron governed justly and wisely,
correcting the worst excesses of his father's

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:54.969
rule, many lords had grown rich off these
excesses and did not approve of Daeron's reforms,

00:03:54.969 --> 00:03:57.599
particularly the peace he'd struck with Dorne.

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:02.099
The malcontents rallied to Daemon and whispered
that he should be king instead of his brother,

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:04.920
whom, thanks to Aegon, many suspected was
a bastard.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.140
At first, Daemon indulged these lords out
of courtesy and vanity.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:14.810
But over time, their grievances and flattery
wore down his objections, along with any sense

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.320
of obligation to the half-brother who had
granted him lands and a wife.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.000
Daemon agreed to claim the throne by right
of birth and, more importantly, arms.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:32.110
A wheel with two hubs will not turn, and a
kingdom with two kings will burn, as the saying

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.110
goes.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:38.580
Not that such a cost stopped anyone with even
the remotest claim and opportunity, much less

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.120
House Blackfyre.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.810
Their rebellions consumed tens of years and
thousands of lives.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:52.310
First Daemon's own, then his son, Daemon the
Second, who reigned for a night.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:58.310
Then another son, Haegon, crowned by Bittersteel,
another legitimized bastard who had founded

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.990
the Golden Company to support the Blackfyre
claim.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:08.090
When Haegon was executed, Bittersteel crowned
Haegon's elder son Daemon the Third, who,

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:13.550
in turn, was slain by the Lord Commander of
the Kingsguard, Ser Duncan the Tall.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:18.840
Finally, Maelys the Monstrous fell to Ser
Barristan Selmy in the War of the Ninepenny

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:25.520
Kings, and the Blackfyre Rebellion ended with
the extinction of the entire line.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.250
As is appropriate.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.389
Fire is only black when it is burned to ash.

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:34.940
Perhaps that was the true problem with the
Targaryens.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.190
The blood of the dragon runs hot and fire
consumes.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:45.319
Perhaps what Westeros needs is a ruler born
not from fire, but from snow.

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:52.729
Jorah Mormont: Aegon Targaryen's Blackfyre
and Visenya's Dark Sister disappeared in Daemon

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:53.729
Blackfyre's rebellion.

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:57.909
Ellaria Sand: A simple word for a simple act.

00:05:57.909 --> 00:06:00.180
And so, of course, men complicate it.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.979
A child born to a wife is a gift from the
gods.

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:10.449
A child born to a mistress or an obedient
servant girl is a bastard, unworthy of its

00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:12.020
father's name.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:17.590
So instead they call the children after the
land where they were born: "Flowers" in the

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:24.970
Reach and "Hill" in the Westerlands, "Stone"
in the Vale and "Storm" in the Stormlands,

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:30.770
"Rivers" in the Riverlands and "Waters" in
the Crownlands, "Pyke" in the Iron Islands,

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:34.870
"Snow" in The North, and in Dorne "Sand".

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:42.699
By these names, everyone can recognize a bastard,
even if his own father won't.

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:47.949
Though sometimes a father with too much gold
and daughters will ask the king to legitimize

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:51.550
a bastard son and give him his family name.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:55.449
If his wife objects, the next one does not.

00:06:55.449 --> 00:07:01.599
But sometimes the gods play their jokes and
later his wife will give him a trueborn son

00:07:01.599 --> 00:07:03.689
of their own.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:12.380
When this happens, well, children die all
the time, so do fathers.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:18.599
Even the beautiful Targaryens had bastards
when brothers tired of their sisters.

00:07:18.599 --> 00:07:22.380
Many took the name Blackfyre after the Conqueror's
own sword.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:28.010
When Aegon the Unworthy legitimized all his
bastards on his deathbed, they rose up against

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.550
his trueborn heir.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:35.479
Westeros bled, Dorne yawned.

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:41.069
For most of Westeros, the Blackfyre Rebellion
only proved what they already knew.

00:07:41.069 --> 00:07:44.259
Bastards are treacherous, born of lust and
shame.

00:07:44.259 --> 00:07:48.650
But in Dorne, lust is not shameful.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:55.240
They know that bastardy does not make a man
more treacherous than another.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.930
Man does not need the help.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:01.889
Bronn: Most boys dream of becoming a Kingsguard.

00:08:01.889 --> 00:08:04.340
Rich boys from good families get the chance.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:09.740
Smart boys stay at home and sing songs about
them instead, opening purses and thighs, because

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:13.290
the Kingsguard isn't really good for much
else.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:18.000
Prince Aemon the Dragonknight may be the most
famous Kingsguard who ever lived.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.800
How did he die?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.539
Defending Aegon the Unworthy from the brothers
of a man whom Aegon fed to his dogs.

00:08:24.539 --> 00:08:26.000
The man's crime?

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.690
Sleeping with one of the many mistresses Aegon
wasn't using, and the man was one of Aegon's

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.710
own Kingsguard.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:37.510
Jaime Lannister: Prince Aemon the Dragonknight,
who wielded the Valyrian sword Dark Sister.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:42.390
He died defending King Aegon the Unworthy
from assassins, though the king had insulted

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:48.470
Aemon throughout his reign and had well earned
his fate because Prince Aemon had sworn our

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.290
oath.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:54.920
Beside the name of Ser Gwayne Corbray, who
dueled the Targaryen bastard Daemon Blackfyre

00:08:54.920 --> 00:09:00.310
for an hour during the Battle of Redgrass
Field though outmatched and grievously wounded,

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.530
because Ser Gwayne had sworn our oath.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:09.940
Viserys Targaryen: But even without our dragons,
we were still the blood of Old Valyria, which

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.140
proved just as dangerous.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:18.020
One of my foolish ancestors didn't see what
separated his bastards from our family proper

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:21.080
and legitimized them all on his deathbed.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:26.700
Adopting the name "Blackfyre," the bastards
proved their nature and tried to seize their

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:27.700
father's kingdom.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:31.160
And when they failed, their sons tried.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:34.060
When their sons failed, their grandsons tried.

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:39.230
Until finally, Ser Barristan the Bold, Knight
of the Kingsguard, slew Maelys the Monstrous

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:44.410
in the War of the Ninepenny Kings, ending
the last of the Blackfyre line.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:50.090
Ultimately, without our dragons and with our
blood diluted by commoners, we failed to see

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.591
the greatest threat growing under our noses.

